Challenge Chosen: Predictive Agriculture for Smallholder Farmers  

Problem Statement & Local Context
Smallholder farmers in Northern Nigeria face unpredictable weather patterns, poor access to timely data, and low yields. They need accurate, easy-to-use tools to make informed decisions on planting, irrigation, and harvesting.

Our Solution
We developed a Real-Time Weather Alert System, using Make.com that integrates with weather APIs to notify farmers daily about rainfall predictions. The system helps farmers plan activities efficiently and reduce losses.

Technologies Used
- Make.com for automation
- Open-Meteo API for weather data
- Google Sheets for data tracking
- HTTP & Email Modules for alerts


Impact & Scalability
- Helps farmers increase productivity by responding to weather conditions.
- Scalable across rural communities with internet access.
- Easy to replicate in other regions using similar API sources.
